VISUAL QA
Viewed each generated sheet, concept, contact, guides and BOTH strips before and after sides retry.
Pass: correct two-view sheet order, true back, side facing directions, full figures and margins, three stacked cloth bundles, empty hands, slim build without added musculature, ivory/slate/red palette, no glow/text/scenery, visible large cloth fold shadows. Arms extend horizontally in front/back; side arms point toward camera rather than reaching forward. All final views share scale/floor.
Qualified: grey background has slight tonal variation, not perfectly uniform. Surface still more faceted than ideal broad smooth low-detail paint. Shadows preserve volume but not an exact copy of concept value grouping. Finials remain relatively sharp. Orthographic side body silhouette is plausible but cage depth/cross-section cannot be proven from painted views.
FAIL: front face still has four visible red stitch marks (small upper one plus three larger), not exactly three. Hood projects into a triangular wedge in side profile and starts too high. Cage is vertically compressed relative to design. Rear waist has an extra upper belt/buckle. Side fingers curl downward rather than staying flat. Lower patch boundaries do not fully describe one consistent wrapped garment.

